## 💡 5. Insights & Findings

✅ **Server Strengths:**

* Managed steady traffic up to **27 req/sec** with excellent stability.
* Rapid recovery after overload shows **good resilience and restart handling**.

⚠️ **Weaknesses:**

* Response time spiked drastically when user load exceeded ~120 concurrent users.
* Timeout errors (794 total) indicate **API throttling or backend bottlenecks**.

💬 **User Impact:** During high stress, users would experience slow or failed responses, but under normal usage the system is fast and reliable.

---

## 🧠 6. Conclusion

The API **performed efficiently under moderate load**, but struggled as concurrency peaked. Once traffic normalized, the system quickly stabilized — suggesting robust but limited scalability.

**In short:**

> ⚙️ Great performance at low to medium load, 🚧 but limited under extreme stress.

**Performance Thresholds:**

* 🟢 Up to ~30 req/sec → Smooth performance
* 🟡 30–60 req/sec → Latency increases noticeably
* 🔴 Beyond 60 req/sec → Timeouts and degradation occur

---

## 🧰 7. Recommendations

| Area                         | Suggestion                                                         |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| 🖥️ **Server Configuration** | Increase thread/concurrency limits, tune timeout values.           |
| 💾 **Backend Optimization**  | Implement caching (Redis, memory cache) for frequent API requests. |
| ⚖️ **Load Balancing**        | Use horizontal scaling with multiple servers or containers.        |
| 📊 **Monitoring**            | Integrate Grafana/Prometheus dashboards for real-time metrics.     |
| 🔍 **Error Handling**        | Add retry logic for ETIMEDOUT scenarios.                           |

